We can finish two different ways that serve the story beats here.

1) Close on the key — quiet, heavy
End by holding the new S16 insert on Dinu’s palm for the full four seconds, then cut to S18’s close on Dinu as rain taps the roof and his face goes still. Storywise this keeps the focus on ownership and the weight of the decision: the key becomes the promise and the burden. Craft-wise it gives a silent, tactile punctuation after the handover, letting the audience sit with the moral consequence before the flashback dissolves.

2) Pull back to both — uncertainty and shared consequence
End by returning to S19 two-shot right after S15 (or trimming S16 shorter), holding the two-shot a beat longer so we see both men in frame as the rain closes in. Storywise this makes the choice communal — the risk is shared, not just Dinu’s — and lets Nimal’s intent and Dinu’s reaction sit together. Craft-wise it preserves the established rhythm of masters and reactions and gives the editor a clear two-shot closing image that reads well against the flashback’s opening.

